  "query_preview": "/Friday through Tuesday/...\nWhile the upper-level ridge is expected to remain over the \nDesert Southwest, flattening of the ridge over the Pacific \nNorthwest is forecast going into the weekend. Hot temperatures \nwill be sticking around, with the larger concern being fire \nweather. Afternoon wind gusts will increase, and despite the \nswitch to west/southwesterly flow aloft, no precipitation is \nexpected. The synoptic pattern looks similar at the beginning of\nnext week as well, however clusters have the upper-level ridge \nretreating east towards the Four Corners region, allowing some \nmoisture to make it into the Great Basin. Time will tell if we \nare fortunate enough for it to make it this far north. Otherwise,\nsmoky conditions will continue from area wildfires.",
